From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:02:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: keep the unmanaged
 radio contract

t8132-laptop.dtsi pulls in t8132-jxxx.dtsi, which puts the Airs'
managed radio contract on &pcie0 and &dart_apcie0 (apple,managed-sids
= <1 2>, Wi-Fi on SID 1 and BT on SID 2, port 0 only). The J604 board
file then restores the contract it shipped on 1.617: iommu-map with
mask 0xff00 (radio functions share SID 1) plus port 2 for the SD card
reader. Both ended up in the J604 tree.

With managed-sids present, apple_pcie_setup_port() runs
apple_pcie_radio_check_cold() on port 0, which maps RID 0x101 through
the board's iommu-map, gets SID 1 instead of 2 and returns -EINVAL
without a message: "Port /soc/pcie@1cb0000000/pci@0,0 setup fail: -22",
no PCIe, no Wi-Fi.

Drop the managed-contract properties on the J604. The resulting tree
differs from the 7.3 package DTB only by these three properties, and the
PCIe/DART nodes then carry the same contract as the 1.617 DTB that boots
the 7.3 kernel with working Wi-Fi.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index fbd1d248e1..769b03e29f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -976,8 +976,18 @@
 	apple,dapf-ranges = /bits/ 64 <0x380704000 0x380704063>, /bits/ 64 <0x380730000 0x380733fff>, /bits/ 64 <0x380e3c000 0x380e3c003>, /bits/ 64 <0x39062c000 0x390648003>, /bits/ 64 <0x501660000 0x501660003>, /bits/ 64 <0x220004000 0x2200162fc>, /bits/ 64 <0x220044000 0x2200562fc>, /bits/ 64 <0x2201c4000 0x2201d62fc>, /bits/ 64 <0x222004000 0x2220162fc>, /bits/ 64 <0x222044000 0x2220562fc>, /bits/ 64 <0x2221c4000 0x2221d62fc>, /bits/ 64 <0x3803c0000 0x3803e4000>, /bits/ 64 <0x382824000 0x382824004>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The J604 runs the unmanaged radio contract that 1.617 shipped: port 0
+ * (radio) and port 2 (SD card reader) both up, RID-to-SID routing owned
+ * by the driver, BT sharing the radio's SID. The managed contract that
+ * t8132-jxxx.dtsi sets for the Airs admits port 0 only and needs the BT
+ * function on its own SID; with this board's iommu-map below it fails
+ * port 0 setup with -EINVAL (no Wi-Fi). Drop it here.
+ */
 &dart_apcie0 {
 	power-domains = <&ps_apcie_gp>;
+	/delete-property/ apple,managed-sids;
+	/delete-property/ apple,dma-range;
 };
 
 &dart_apcie2 {
@@ -986,6 +996,7 @@
 };
 
 &pcie0 {
+	/delete-property/ apple,managed-sids;
 	power-domains = <&ps_apcie_phy_sw>;
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pcie_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-- 
